While the baseline CRAP measurement runs, let me study the code in detail.

### 1. `gitPushGuard.commitMessageText` (CRAP 38)

```js
function commitMessageText(args, fileContents) {
   var parts = [];
   var i = 0;
   while (i < args.length) {
       var a = args[i];
       if (a === '-m' || a === '--message' || /^-[a-zA-Z]*m$/.test(a)) {
           if (i + 1 < args.length) { parts.push(args[i + 1]); i += 2; continue; }
           i += 1; continue;
       }
       if (a.indexOf('--message=') === 0) { parts.push(a.substring('--message='.length)); i += 1; continue; }
       if (a.indexOf('-m') === 0 && a.length > 2 && a.indexOf('--') !== 0) {
           // joined form: -m"text"
           parts.push(a.substring(2));
           i += 1; continue;
       }
       if (a === '-F' || a === '--file' || /^-[a-zA-Z]*F$/.test(a)) {
           if (i + 1 < args.length && fileContents && fileContents[args[i + 1]]) {
               parts.push(fileContents[args[i + 1]]);
           }
           i += 2; continue;
       }
       if (a.indexOf('--file=') === 0) {
           var f = a.substring('--file='.length);
           if (fileContents && fileContents[f]) parts.push(fileContents[f]);
           i += 1; continue;
       }
       i += 1;
   }
   return parts.join('\n');
}
``

Branches:
1. `-m`-style flag (exact or combined short): has next arg → push, i+=2; no next → i+=1
2. `--message=VALUE` → push value
3. joined `-mTEXT` → push text
4. `-F`-style: next in fileContents → push content; i+=2 always
5. `--file=VALUE`: in map → push
6. other: skip

To reduce CRAP: extract pure helpers. E.g.:

- `shortMessageFlag(a)` — matches `-m`, `--message`, `/^-[a-zA-Z]*m$/`
- `messageFlagValue(a, args, i, fileContents)`?

